s (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 10th District is an open seat after Republican John James left to run for governor, and it sits in territory that leans about three points Republican at baseline. With the national political environment favoring Democrats this cycle, the fundamentals tilt slightly toward Democrat Christina Hines over Republican Mike Bouchard Jr. Expert raters are split: several call it a tossup, while others, including Silver Bulletin, Split Ticket, and The Economist, rate it a Democratic flip. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket price Hines around 65% to win.\n\nThe polling record is thin and dated. The only usable survey, a Democratic-sponsored August poll of likely voters, showed the race tied at 45-45, and a House Majority PAC memo also described a tie. Hines has raised more money than Bouchard and benefits from a $1 million Giffords PAC investment, while Bouchard, a Bronze Star veteran, entered the race after returning from Iraq. The race remains genuinely competitive, with a modest Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6628, "margin": 2.54}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6831, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.623, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5903, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6399, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6806, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7119, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6799, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6842, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6979, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6212, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6412, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", 